            <ArticleTitle>Screening for hypertension: a rational approach.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>67-72</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A strategy for the control of hypertension in communities is presented as a staged program. Stage I consists of the evaluation and improvement of hypertension management in health care facilities. Stage II entails case-finding in health care facilities. Finally, Stage III involves targeted screening in the community. While isolated screening programs have been justly labeled &quot;irrational&quot;, such a sequential strategy represents a highly rational approach to the community control of hypertension.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
